{"ts":"2026-08-16T01:48:01.075Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7752eeaf5a7145ec7bd42151","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-16T01:48:01.075Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-16T01:48:01.075Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Starting implementation. Plan: `pm rl invalidate <id>` walks the host-owned relationship graph (`client.graph(\"impact\", {id}, {direction: \"incoming\"})`) so invalidation is genuine reachability over the `dependencies` edges pm already stores — Run→Environment, EvalResult→Run/Benchmark, Transfer→both environments — not a re-implementation in pm-rl. It classifies affected items into EvalResult/Transfer/Run and reports the exact path for each. Adversarial tests: cycle, dangling dep id, zero-overlap runs, identical-metrics-different-config, and cross-environment-version refusal for compare."}]}],"before_hash":"31eeeb6fcd5279c6e0a7819b0478ac44b6ed9c86e596f8f1ca36d60070afc99e","after_hash":"b6188a86fcfaaa4da378353f677eb0e95da546b78ded81d83028f59c6d9cfb8d","item_hash_version":2}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T02:27:55.738Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7752eeaf5a7145ec7bd42151","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-16T02:27:55.738Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Critical finding while implementing: the host's `pm graph impact` registers the `related` kind (what `--dep` records) as an UNDIRECTED relationship, so the blast-radius walk crosses a Transfer's second environment into the other version's runs — reporting results whose provenance does not derive from the changed version. Invalidation is directional data flow (a result derives FROM its dependencies), so the walk runs over the `dependencies` arrays pm itself stores (one `list --fields id,type,dependencies` read) with a directed BFS toward dependents. pm-rl still stores no graph of its own: the edge data, kinds, and dangling references all come from pm's items. Exactness proven on a real fixture: invalidating env v1 returns exactly v1's subtree plus the shared transfer, never v2/v3's runs."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-16T02:27:55.738Z"}],"before_hash":"b6188a86fcfaaa4da378353f677eb0e95da546b78ded81d83028f59c6d9cfb8d","after_hash":"bd9c444bc2a2da1318c7e6a345d1ed583ab96af1dccdeb20bc45889f4942b3da","item_hash_version":2}
